(https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html). It combines code under GPL (version 2 or later), GPL-3 and
MIT, all of which can be distributed under version 3, the way the immunedeconv
package declares the licence of the methods it collects. This file records where
the code and data of the natively implemented methods come from.

Fifteen methods are implemented in the package: abis, seqimmucc, base, timer,
estimate, immucellai2, spatialdecon_safetme, immucellai_mouse, consensus_tme,
xcell, mcp_counter, mmcp_counter, imsig, quantiseq and xcell2.

The other methods are not part of this package: their original packages are
installed separately into a private library and run in separate R processes
(bulkdeconv_install()); their licences are listed in the registry
(bulkdeconv_methods()$license) and reported when a method runs.

CODE
  R/native.R, R/native2.R and R/native3.R are ports of the algorithms below, written so that it gives the
  same numbers as the original code. Sources:
  - seq-ImmuCC LLSR: seqImmuCC_LLSR.R in omnideconv/immunedeconv (GPL-2),
    stated there to be provided by the seq-ImmuCC authors.
    Chen Z, et al. Front Immunol 2018, doi:10.3389/fimmu.2018.01286
  - ABIS: server.R of the ABIS application (github.com/giannimonaco/ABIS),
    in the form adapted in omnideconv/immunedeconv (GPL-2).
    Monaco G, et al. Cell Rep 2019, doi:10.1016/j.celrep.2019.01.041
  - BASE: code adapted from Varn FS, et al. Cancer Res 2017,
    doi:10.1158/0008-5472.CAN-16-2490, in the form adapted in
    omnideconv/immunedeconv (GPL-2). The cumulative sums are vectorised.
  - TIMER: github.com/hanfeisun/TIMER (GPL-2.0), itself adapted from the
    original TIMER source (cistrome.org/TIMER).
    Li B, et al. Genome Biol 2016, doi:10.1186/s13059-016-1028-7
    Constrained regression: Abbas AR, et al. PLoS One 2009.
  - ESTIMATE: tidyestimate 1.1.1 (GPL >= 2; Aragaki K), which packages the
    ESTIMATE algorithm of Yoshihara K, et al. Nat Commun 2013,
    doi:10.1038/ncomms3612 (copyright holder of the ESTIMATE package: P. Roebuck).
  - ImmuCellAI 2.0: R-package/ImmuCellAI2.0 of github.com/GuoBioinfoLab/ImmuCellAI-2.0
    at commit 0135016 (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Jingmin Yang).
  - SpatialDecon 1.20.1 (MIT, Copyright (c) 2021 NanoString Technologies, Inc.;
    Danaher P, et al. Nat Commun 2022, doi:10.1038/s41467-022-28020-5), with the
    objective and gradient of logNormReg::lognlm() (GPL; Muggeo VMR) written out
    following that package, for the log-normal least-squares fit.
  - ImmuCellAI-mouse 0.1.5: github.com/BioInfoCloud/ImmuCellAI_mouse at commit
    b9fc2e7 (MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 Yun Sen; Miao Y-R, et al. Adv Sci 2023,
    doi:10.1002/advs.202300878).
  - ConsensusTME 0.0.1.9000 (GPL-3; Jimenez-Sanchez A, et al. Cancer Res 2019,
    doi:10.1158/0008-5472.CAN-18-3711), github.com/cansysbio/ConsensusTME at 6e14ba3.
  - xCell 1.1.0 (GPL-3; Aran D, et al. Genome Biol 2017, doi:10.1186/s13059-017-1349-1),
    github.com/dviraran/xCell at 20e2919.
  - xCell2 1.2.3 (GPL >= 3; Almog Angel and Dvir Aran), Bioconductor 3.22,
    commit 38ae014; inference only, in R/xcell2.R. The rank normalisation
    follows Foroutan M, et al. BMC Bioinformatics 2018,
    doi:10.1186/s12859-018-2435-4.
  - MCPcounter 1.2.0 (GPL-3; Becht E, et al. Genome Biol 2016, doi:10.1186/s13059-016-1070-5),
    github.com/ebecht/MCPcounter at b6eac73 (marker table from Signatures/genes.txt).
  - mMCP-counter 1.1.0 (GPL-3; Petitprez F, et al. Genome Med 2020,
    doi:10.1186/s13073-020-00783-w), github.com/cit-bioinfo/mMCP-counter at cec6971.
  - imsig 1.1.3 (GPL-3; Nirmal AJ, et al. Cancer Immunol Res 2018,
    doi:10.1158/2326-6066.CIR-17-0568).
  - quantiseqr 1.18.0 (GPL-3; Federico A, Ponzoni L, Marini F), the R implementation of
    quanTIseq (Finotello F, et al. Genome Med 2019, doi:10.1186/s13073-019-0638-6); the
    constrained least squares uses the quadprog package.
  - ssGSEA follows Barbie DA, et al. Nature 2009 and Hanzelmann S, et al. BMC
    Bioinformatics 2013 and is checked against GSVA; the non-negative least
    squares routine follows Lawson & Hanson (1974).
  immunedeconv: Sturm G, Finotello F, et al. Bioinformatics 2019;
  Merotto L, et al. Bioinform Adv 2024. It is not installed or called by
  bulkdeconv; data-raw/make_fixtures.R uses it once to record the expected
  output of the original implementations for the tests.

DATA (inst/extdata/, built by data-raw/build_extdata.R. The first six files are taken
from omnideconv/immunedeconv at commit e625e6c28ed14a30f9f40f159925cc9f0df4fa49;
the rest from the packages named, at the versions named.)
  seqimmucc/sig_matr_seqImmuCC.txt   signature matrix of seq-ImmuCC.
  abis/sigmatrixRNAseq.txt           ABIS RNA-seq signature matrix.
  base/compendium.rds                BASE mouse cell compendium (up/down
                                     weight sets). Rounded to 6 decimals
                                     (largest change 5e-7) and stored
                                     xz-compressed to reduce its size.
  base/cell_correspondance.txt       mapping of compendium samples to cell types.
  timer/immune_reference.rds         curated immune-cell expression reference
                                     of TIMER (public sorted-cell expression
                                     profiles).
  timer/markers_by_cancer.rds        TIMER marker genes per cancer type, the 32
                                     precalculated files as one list.
  estimate/estimate_data.rds         ESTIMATE common genes and the stromal and
                                     immune signatures, from tidyestimate 1.1.1.
  spatialdecon/safeTME.rds           SAFE-TME cell-profile matrix, from
                                     SpatialDecon 1.20.1.
  immucellai_mouse/reference.rds     marker expression, marker lists and
                                     correction matrices, from ImmuCellAI-mouse.
  consensus_tme/gene_sets.rds        ConsensusTME consensus gene sets (TCGA types
                                     and unfiltered).
  xcell/xcell_data.rds               xCell signatures (489), gene list, fitted
                                     transformation parameters, spill-over matrix.
  xcell2/*.rds                       Nine pre-trained references from xCell2
                                     1.2.3, extracted by data-raw/build_xcell2.R.
                                     Preset names and origins are in the registry;
                                     LM22 is trained on the Newman et al. reference.
  mcp_counter/markers.rds            MCP-counter marker genes (genes.txt).
  mmcp_counter/signatures_GCRm39.rds mMCP-counter signatures (GCRm39).
  imsig/sig.rds                      ImSig signature genes per cell type.
  quantiseq/til10.rds                TIL10 signature matrix, mRNA scaling, genes to
                                     remove, and the HGNC table (2017-04-18) used to
                                     re-annotate gene symbols; from quantiseqr.
  immucellai2/reference_markers.rds  the 53-state reference restricted to the
                                     5510 marker genes (the package reads a 41 MB
                                     text file and keeps these rows), and the
                                     marker list; from ImmuCellAI 2.0.

  All reference files listed above are part of the source distribution. They
  are distributed as published and as already distributed in immunedeconv and
  xCell2, with attribution to their authors.

